The LGPL engines
  OpenCascade and PlaneGCS are shipped as separate files (occt.wasm.gz, planegcs.wasm) and loaded
  at run time, so you can swap in your own builds. PlaneGCS source: https://github.com/FreeCAD/FreeCAD
  (src/Mod/Sketcher/App/planegcs) and https://github.com/Salusoft89/planegcs.
  The OpenCascade kernel is shipped as a separate file, dist/occt.wasm.gz, loaded at run time.
  You may replace it with your own build of replicad-opencascadejs. Source:
  https://github.com/sgenoud/replicad (packages/replicad-opencascadejs) and
  https://dev.opencascade.org. Open CASCADE Technology is licensed LGPL-2.1 with the
  Open CASCADE exception.

Fonts
  Jost: Copyright 2020 The Jost Project Authors (https://github.com/indestructible-type/Jost).
  IBM Plex: Copyright 2019 IBM Corp. Both under the SIL Open Font License 1.1, embedded
  unmodified (Latin subsets, as packaged by Fontsource). For PDF embedding the build converts the
  same WOFF2 files to TrueType (dist/fonts/*.ttf) without changing any glyph; exported PDFs carry
  subsets of them, which the OFL permits.

Names and marks
  "KERF", "AKA IND", "AKAIND", "AI² Lab", the KERF block mark and the AKA mark (src/assets/
  aka-mark.svg) identify the project and its publisher. The AGPL gives you the code, not the names
  or marks: if you ship a modified version, please call it something else and remove the marks so
  nobody mistakes it for an official release. "Rhino" and ".3dm" are used only to name a file
  format KERF can read; KERF is not affiliated with Robert McNeel & Associates.
